0..125 Comment "/// The default build stage: a package\'s `gandr.toml` body, rendered by a gandr function from its model\'s fields and modules."
126..129 Comment "///"
130..362 Comment "/// A package\'s own build stage is to write its manifest, the checker\'s fixed rule its default. Before the checker can run a stage, this source shows the default spelled in gandr: each run is the body of a manifest the tree commits."
363..366 Comment "///"
367..639 Comment "/// `body` reads the name, the version and the module list, and writes the `[package]` table as the checker does. The checker keeps the header and its BLAKE3 digest, which only it computes. A name holding a quote is not escaped here: that needs the characters of a string."
640..643 Comment "///"
